\flagvar{\conjpart{\lambda}}
  \mathrm {Fl}_{\lambda '} — the partial flag variety of the
  conjugate type; \conjpart{\lambda}
  \lambda ' is conjugation of partitions.

\flagvar{\conjpart{\lambda}}
  \mathrm {Fl}_{\lambda '} — the partial flag variety of the
  conjugate type; \conjpart{\lambda}
  \lambda ' is conjugation of partitions.

\resform{P}{A}{B}
  \operatorname {tr}([P, A]B) — the residue form at a drop point: the
  semi-local avatar of the same pairing.

\adP{P} \operatorname {ad}_{P} — the commutator
  map on the pencil's \mathbb {P}^1;
  \centsheaf{P} \mathcal {C}_{P} — its
  kernel, the centralizer sheaf, whose Euler characteristic
  \euler{\centsheaf{P}}
  \chi (\mathcal {C}_{P}) is the Riemann--Roch budget.

\Nstrict N_{\mathrm {strict}} — the nullity of
  the pairing on honest strict Hom-triples;
  \Nweak N_{\mathrm {weak}} — its
  belowdiagonal-relaxed companion;
  \Nz N_z — the centralizer-side count.

\Ltwo (L2) — decreasing monomial
  germs are vacuous, a theorem;
  \Lthree (L3) — refuted.

\Mlaw the M-law — the argmax count;
  \TOPX (TOP-X) — the rigidity of maximal
  modality, which is what carries the M-law across to \operatorname {lc} \kappa (U_{n}).

\mathcal {O} — the nilpotent orbit \mathcal {O}_{\lambda }
  (\orbit) and the structure sheaf
  \mathcal {O} (\structsheaf).
